# Reviewer Response

Use the reviewer comments supplied by the user or read the given file.
Save the draft in `notes/reviewer_responses/` (for example
`round1.md`). For each comment, write:

1. the reviewer comment quoted verbatim
2. a concise, courteous response
3. the manuscript change made or proposed, quoted
4. its location (file and section)

Match each response to the evidence: quote new numbers as
`{{v:key}}` (see paper-values) and cite only keys in
`bibliography/references.bib`. Flag comments that need new analyses or
data the user must provide instead of promising results.

Do not edit the manuscript until the user has reviewed the draft and
asks for the revision.
